 "_doc": [
  "Pokémon from Unova (Rowan's sixth question, PFLAG_UNOVA; the user 2026-11-23, notes/DECISIONS.md; notes/UNOVA.md).",
  "b2tools/unova.py turns this plan into each version's slot edits (--report prints them, --check checks the rules); the build",
  "(b2tools/patches/unova.py) writes them into a/1/2/7 for the decomp's resident/unova.c. Hand-made: the kinds of each area.",
  "areas: zone name (fnmatch patterns allowed; every zone of the version with wild Pokémon must match one) -> group -> kinds.",
  "  Groups: grass (land and caves), surf, good (Good Rod), super (Super Rod); the Old Rod never changes.",
  "  A kind: SPECIES (that species), ~SPECIES (its family: the last stage the slot's lowest level reaches by levelling),",
  "  @SPECIES (a version pair, \"pairs\": Pearl the first, Diamond the second, Platinum both), a trailing * = rare (one",
  "  small slot). The slots are picked by unova.py (about a quarter of each group; every Sinnoh Pokémon keeps a slot).",
  "pairs: White's side (Pearl) -> Black's side (Diamond). After the Champion each of Pearl and Diamond gets the other's",
  "  in one more slot of the same area.",
  "starters: species -> the area of its one 1 % grass slot (the same in every version).",
  "teams: the Gym Leaders', Elite Four's and Champion's first battles with the option (b2tools/unova.py teams)."
 ],
